on":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}],"priceRange":"$$"},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Arkansas Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/#webpage","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/","name":"Insurance Claim Glossary | ACV, RCV, Umpire & More","description":"Insurance claim glossary in plain English: actual cash value, replacement cost, holdback, appraisal award, umpire, ARRUA, ice dams and 40+ more terms.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-12","primaryImageOfPage":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/#primaryimage"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/#definedtermset"}},{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/#primaryimage","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp","contentUrl":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp","width":960,"height":640,"caption":"Calculator on printed charts beside a laptop"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Claim glossary","item":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/"}],"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"DefinedTermSet","name":"Insurance claim glossary","hasDefinedTerm":[{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Actual cash value (ACV)","description":"The value of damaged property at the time of loss, commonly replacement cost minus depreciation."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Additional living expense (ALE)","description":"Coverage for the increase in living costs when a covered loss makes your home unlivable."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Amount of loss","description":"The dollar value of covered damage. It is the question an appraisal panel decides."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Appraisal clause","description":"The policy condition that lets either side demand appraisal when they disagree on the amount of loss."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Appraisal award","description":"The written decision setting the amount of loss, binding when signed by two of the three panel members."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"ARRUA","description":"The Arkansas Rural Risk Underwriting Association, the state’s statutory residual market for basic property coverage in designated rural areas."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Arkansas Insurance Department","description":"The state agency that licenses insurers, reviews filings and handles consumer complaints."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Coinsurance","description":"A commercial policy clause that reduces payment if the property was insured below a set percentage of its value."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Collateral damage","description":"Dents and marks on gutters, vents, AC units and similar items that help confirm a hailstorm’s size and date."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Contents","description":"Personal property such as furniture, clothing and electronics, usually Coverage C on a homeowner policy."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Coverage A","description":"Dwelling coverage for the house itself on a homeowner policy."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Coverage B","description":"Other structures coverage for detached garages, fences, sheds and similar buildings."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Declarations page","description":"The summary page listing your coverages, limits, deductibles and policy period."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Debris removal","description":"Coverage for removing damaged property and, within limits, fallen trees."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Depreciation","description":"The reduction in value due to age, wear and condition. Recoverable depreciation can be paid after repairs."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Drip edge","description":"Metal flashing at roof edges that directs water into gutters. Often missing from roof estimates."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Earth movement exclusion","description":"A standard exclusion for earthquakes, landslides and similar events unless an endorsement adds coverage."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Endorsement","description":"A form that adds to, removes from or changes a policy’s coverage."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Glaze ice","description":"The clear, dense ice formed by freezing rain, responsible for most ice storm damage."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Holdback","description":"Recoverable depreciation withheld from the first payment until repairs are completed."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Ice dam","description":"A ridge of ice at the eaves that traps meltwater, which can then back up under shingles."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Impartial","description":"Without bias toward either side. Most appraisal clauses require appraisers and umpires to be impartial."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Line item","description":"A single entry in an estimate, with a description, quantity and unit price."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Matching","description":"Whether replacement materials reasonably match undamaged materials in color, texture and profile."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Mitigation","description":"Reasonable steps to prevent further damage after a loss, such as tarping or water extraction."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"New Madrid Seismic Zone","description":"A seismic zone affecting northeast Arkansas. Earthquake damage generally requires separate coverage."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Ordinance or law coverage","description":"Coverage for added costs of meeting current building codes during repair."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Overhead and profit (O&P)","description":"A general contractor’s charge for coordinating multiple trades, often 10% overhead and 10% profit."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Percentage deductible","description":"A deductible calculated as a percentage of the dwelling limit, common for wind and hail."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Pitch","description":"A roof’s steepness, expressed as inches of rise per 12 inches of run, such as 6/12."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Proof of loss","description":"A sworn statement of the amount claimed, often required within a set time after the insurer requests it."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Replacement cost value (RCV)","description":"The cost to repair or replace damaged property with materials of like kind and quality, without deduction for depreciation."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Roofing square","description":"100 square feet of roof surface, the standard unit for roofing estimates."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Scope of loss","description":"The list of damaged items and the work needed to repair them."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Steep charge","description":"Extra labor cost for working on roofs above a certain pitch, commonly 7/12 or 8/12."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Straight-line wind","description":"Damaging wind from thunderstorms that is not rotating, sometimes exceeding tornado-strength speeds."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Suit limitation","description":"The policy clause limiting how long you have to file a lawsuit against the insurer."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Supplement","description":"A request for additional payment for items missed or discovered after the original estimate."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Test square","description":"A 10-by-10-foot area on a roof slope used to count and document hail hits."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Umpire","description":"The neutral third member of an appraisal panel who decides items the two appraisers can’t resolve."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Wind-driven rain","description":"Rain forced into a building by wind. Coverage often depends on whether wind first created an opening."},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","name":"Xactimate","description":"Widely used estimating software for property insurance claims, with regional price lists."}],"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/insurance-claim-glossary/#definedtermset"}]}</script>
</head>
