<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li>Claim glossary</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker kicker-l">Reference</p><h1>Insurance Claim Glossary: Plain-English Terms</h1><p class="lede">42 terms you’ll meet in policies, estimates and appraisal awards, defined simply. Type to filter.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap two"><article class="prose"><div class="gfilter"><label for="gloss-q">Search the glossary</label><input id="gloss-q" type="search" placeholder="Try “holdback” or “umpire”" autocomplete="off"><p class="note" data-gcount>42 terms</p></div><div class="az"><a href="#g-A">A</a><a href="#g-C">C</a><a href="#g-D">D</a><a href="#g-E">E</a><a href="#g-G">G</a><a href="#g-H">H</a><a href="#g-I">I</a><a href="#g-L">L</a><a href="#g-M">M</a><a href="#g-N">N</a><a href="#g-O">O</a><a href="#g-P">P</a><a href="#g-R">R</a><a href="#g-S">S</a><a href="#g-T">T</a><a href="#g-U">U</a><a href="#g-W">W</a><a href="#g-X">X</a></div><dl class="glossary"><div class="term" id="g-A"><dt>Actual cash value (ACV)</dt><dd>The value of damaged property at the time of loss, commonly replacement cost minus depreciation.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Additional living expense (ALE)</dt><dd>Coverage for the increase in living costs when a covered loss makes your home unlivable.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Amount of loss</dt><dd>The dollar value of covered damage. It is the question an appraisal panel decides.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Appraisal award</dt><dd>The written decision setting the amount of loss, binding when signed by two of the three panel members.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Appraisal clause</dt><dd>The policy condition that lets either side demand appraisal when they disagree on the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Arkansas Insurance Department</dt><dd>The state agency that licenses insurers, reviews filings and handles consumer complaints.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>ARRUA</dt><dd>The Arkansas Rural Risk Underwriting Association, the state’s statutory residual market for basic property coverage in designated rural areas.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-C"><dt>Coinsurance</dt><dd>A commercial policy clause that reduces payment if the property was insured below a set percentage of its value.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Collateral damage</dt><dd>Dents and marks on gutters, vents, AC units and similar items that help confirm a hailstorm’s size and date.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Contents</dt><dd>Personal property such as furniture, clothing and electronics, usually Coverage C on a homeowner policy.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Coverage A</dt><dd>Dwelling coverage for the house itself on a homeowner policy.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Coverage B</dt><dd>Other structures coverage for detached garages, fences, sheds and similar buildings.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-D"><dt>Debris removal</dt><dd>Coverage for removing damaged property and, within limits, fallen trees.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Declarations page</dt><dd>The summary page listing your coverages, limits, deductibles and policy period.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Depreciation</dt><dd>The reduction in value due to age, wear and condition. Recoverable depreciation can be paid after repairs.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Drip edge</dt><dd>Metal flashing at roof edges that directs water into gutters. Often missing from roof estimates.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-E"><dt>Earth movement exclusion</dt><dd>A standard exclusion for earthquakes, landslides and similar events unless an endorsement adds coverage.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Endorsement</dt><dd>A form that adds to, removes from or changes a policy’s coverage.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-G"><dt>Glaze ice</dt><dd>The clear, dense ice formed by freezing rain, responsible for most ice storm damage.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-H"><dt>Holdback</dt><dd>Recoverable depreciation withheld from the first payment until repairs are completed.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-I"><dt>Ice dam</dt><dd>A ridge of ice at the eaves that traps meltwater, which can then back up under shingles.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Impartial</dt><dd>Without bias toward either side. Most appraisal clauses require appraisers and umpires to be impartial.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-L"><dt>Line item</dt><dd>A single entry in an estimate, with a description, quantity and unit price.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-M"><dt>Matching</dt><dd>Whether replacement materials reasonably match undamaged materials in color, texture and profile.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Mitigation</dt><dd>Reasonable steps to prevent further damage after a loss, such as tarping or water extraction.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-N"><dt>New Madrid Seismic Zone</dt><dd>A seismic zone affecting northeast Arkansas. Earthquake damage generally requires separate coverage.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-O"><dt>Ordinance or law coverage</dt><dd>Coverage for added costs of meeting current building codes during repair.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Overhead and profit (O&amp;P)</dt><dd>A general contractor’s charge for coordinating multiple trades, often 10% overhead and 10% profit.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-P"><dt>Percentage deductible</dt><dd>A deductible calculated as a percentage of the dwelling limit, common for wind and hail.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Pitch</dt><dd>A roof’s steepness, expressed as inches of rise per 12 inches of run, such as 6/12.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Proof of loss</dt><dd>A sworn statement of the amount claimed, often required within a set time after the insurer requests it.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-R"><dt>Replacement cost value (RCV)</dt><dd>The cost to repair or replace damaged property with materials of like kind and quality, without deduction for depreciation.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Roofing square</dt><dd>100 square feet of roof surface, the standard unit for roofing estimates.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-S"><dt>Scope of loss</dt><dd>The list of damaged items and the work needed to repair them.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Steep charge</dt><dd>Extra labor cost for working on roofs above a certain pitch, commonly 7/12 or 8/12.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Straight-line wind</dt><dd>Damaging wind from thunderstorms that is not rotating, sometimes exceeding tornado-strength speeds.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Suit limitation</dt><dd>The policy clause limiting how long you have to file a lawsuit against the insurer.</dd></div><div class="term"><dt>Supplement</dt><dd>A request for additional payment for items missed or discovered after the original estimate.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-T"><dt>Test square</dt><dd>A 10-by-10-foot area on a roof slope used to count and document hail hits.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-U"><dt>Umpire</dt><dd>The neutral third member of an appraisal panel who decides items the two appraisers can’t resolve.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-W"><dt>Wind-driven rain</dt><dd>Rain forced into a building by wind. Coverage often depends on whether wind first created an opening.</dd></div><div class="term" id="g-X"><dt>Xactimate</dt><dd>Widely used estimating software for property insurance claims, with regional price lists.</dd></div></dl></article>
<aside class="aside"><div class="sbox sbox-call"><h2 class="sbox-t">Talk it through, free</h2><p>A short call tells you whether appraisal fits your claim, or whether something else would serve you better.</p><a class="sbox-tel" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> +1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-white btn-block" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="sbox"><h2 class="sbox-t">Resources</h2><ul class="sbox-list"><li><a href="/appraisal-process-explained/">Appraisal process<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/faq/">FAQ<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/insurance-claim-glossary/" aria-current="page">Claim glossary<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-guides/">Appraisal guides<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></aside></div>
